359	MIE286H1	Probability and Statistics	0.5	36.6L/12.2T	A course in probability and statistics for Engineering Science students focusing on building solid probabilistic and statistical foundations both mathematically and in terms of engineering application. Topics include: sample space, events, definitions of probability, conditional probability, Bayes' theorem, important classes of discrete and continuous random variables and their distributions, joint, conditional, and marginal distributions, expectation, moment generating and characteristic functions, transformations of random variables, central limit theorem and approximations. Graphical methods, quantile plots, point and interval estimation of population parameters, method of maximum likelihood. Hypothesis testing, simple and multiple regression, correlation analysis, and introduction to Bayesian statistics.	\N	\N	CHE223H1,CME263H1,ECE286H1,MIE236H1,MIE237H1,MIE231H1,MSE238H1,STA286H1orSTA257H1	\N	42.7 (Fall), 42.7 (Winter), 85.4 (Full Year)	AEESCBASE: Winter Session - Year 2
360	MIE301H1	Kinematics and Dynamics of Machines	0.5	38.4L/25.6T/38.4P	Classifications of mechanisms, velocity, acceleration and force analysis, graphical and computer-oriented methods, gears, geartrains, cams, flywheels, mechanism dynamics.Instruction and assessment of engineering communication that will form part of an ongoing design portfolio.	MIE100H1	\N	\N	\N	67.1 (Fall), 67.1 (Winter), 134.2 (Full Year)	AEMECBASC: Fall Session - Year 3AEMINRAM: Introductory Courses
